# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-7 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-7 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-7 throughout (B7 built it).
# M7: the S3a matrix gate on the PRODUCTION profile: four users at 4,096 / 16,384 / 32,768 / 60,000 prompt tokens, 512 out, every arm
# IDENTICAL to its solo run (first run and one rerun, the policy's). On tp4-serve-6 the same matrix passed as the gate-only profile
# c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace; this repeats it as c2-packed-tp4 itself, so the exactness claim is made for the profile that is served.
# The gate driver adds its own extent audit to the arms, as it did for the strace arm; the production environment is otherwise untouched.
# READ the report: POLICY PASS, every matrix arm identical to solo, no refuse_round, no idle commit, no audit mismatch, no stall-watch
# dump, and the arms' profile line is c2-packed-tp4.
# Duration (estimate): 60 min. Stop rule: any non-identical arm or a policy failure stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-7
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=4096,16384,32768,60000
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=512
C2_GATE_JIT=record
